@RedmondBarry7 I don't accept your framing. There is no such thing as "surface level" merit. You use language in a very disingenuous way. You are trying to discount actual merit to slip in other metrics as if they were a form of merit.

You are also trying to obfuscate the very obvious selection criteria that has been characteristic of DEI programs like race, sex etc. 

We collectively fell for this once, we won't fall for it again.
